{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalLagrangianUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalLagrangianUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QDifferentialGeometry","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangian.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangian.unique","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian-unique.lean#L26-L54","doc":"**Uniqueness of the categorical Lagrangian.**\n\nGiven fixed Dirac operator, state, and costate, the Lagrangian\n`𝒟_∇² + ψ* ⊗ 𝒟_∇ψ` is uniquely determined: the `lagrangian` morphism is\nforced by [`def:categorical-lagrangian`]'s `lagrangian_formula`, so two\nsuch Lagrangians are equal.\n\nThis replaces the earlier `axiom … : Subsingleton (CategoricalLagrangian …)`,\nwhich was **false** (the structure has free fields).  Uniqueness holds only\nconditionally on shared data — exactly the narrative claim. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-lagrangian-unique","label":"prop:categorical-lagrangian-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lagrangian-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}